Step 1 - Enumerate RPC Services
nmap -sT -Pn -sV --script rpcinfo -p111 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com

If rpcinfo script is unavailable:

rpcinfo -p iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 2 - Enumerate NFS Shares
nmap -sT -Pn --script nfs-showmount -p2049 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com

If unavailable

showmount -e iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 3 - List Files in NFS
nmap -sT -Pn --script nfs-ls -p2049 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 4 - NFS Filesystem Information
nmap -sT -Pn --script nfs-statfs -p2049 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 5 - Docker Enumeration
nmap -sT -Pn -sV -p2376 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com

Then

curl -k https://iapp192644.croydon.ms.com:2376/version

Then

curl -k https://iapp192644.croydon.ms.com:2376/info

Then

curl -k https://iapp192644.croydon.ms.com:2376/images/json

If any of these return JSON without authentication, that's a serious misconfiguration.

Step 6 - Banner Grabbing
nmap -sT -sV --version-all iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 7 - Scan Only Open Ports with NSE
nmap -sT -Pn -sC -p22,111,1914,2049,2376,20048 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 8 - Aggressive Service Detection
nmap -sT -Pn -A -p22,111,1914,2049,2376,20048 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com

-A is supported with -sT; OS detection may be limited without Npcap, but version detection and NSE scripts can still run.

Step 9 - Scan High RPC Ports
nmap -sT -Pn -sV -p6165,14141,15305,19937,19997,20048,21949,25215,32623,32733,48476,48966 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 10 - Try Default Vulnerability Scripts
nmap -sT -Pn --script default,vuln -p22,111,2049,2376 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com

If your Nmap 7.40 doesn't include the vuln category, this may fail.

Step 11 - Check Docker TLS
openssl s_client -connect iapp192644.croydon.ms.com:2376

If OpenSSL is available.

Step 12 - Check SSH Algorithms
nmap -sT -Pn --script ssh2-enum-algos -p22 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
Step 13 - Check SSH Host Keys
nmap -sT -Pn --script ssh-hostkey -p22 iapp192644.croydon.ms.com
